cl-store on Evergreen Common Lisp (EGCL).  Sean Ross's cl-store (the
serialization library zacl uses for AllegroServe's fasl-write and
fasl-read), Quicklisp release 2023-02-14, refuses to load on a Lisp it
does not know.  This adds EGCL to its list with :egcl as the backend
directory name.  EGCL keeps its slot-introspection functions in CL-USER,
as atgreen's closer-mop port does, so the package imports them from
there; ensure-class, generic-function-name, compute-slots and the
class-direct-* readers beyond class-direct-slots do not exist on EGCL
yet and stay cl-store's own undefined symbols (reached only when storing
class metaobjects themselves).  get-slot-details specializes on t, as on
ECL and Clasp.  egcl/custom.lisp stores structures (specialized on
structure-object, since EGCL does not expose structure-class as a class)
and defines no special-float table, because EGCL signals on overflow and
division by zero instead of producing infinities.

The pipeline's deps job (.gitlab-ci.yml) applies this to the dist's
cl-store with patch -p1 for the EGCL test job; the other Lisps are not
affected by it.  Owed upstream (github.com/skypher/cl-store).

diff -ruN a/cl-store.asd b/cl-store.asd
--- a/cl-store.asd
+++ b/cl-store.asd
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@

 (in-package #:cl-store.system)

-#-(or lispworks mcl cmu clisp sbcl allegro ecl openmcl abcl clasp)
+#-(or lispworks mcl cmu clisp sbcl allegro ecl openmcl abcl clasp egcl)
 (error "This is an unsupported lisp implementation.
 Currently only MCL, OpenMCL, Lispworks, CMUCL, SBCL,
 CLISP, ECL, AllegroCL and CLASP are supported.")
@@ -20,7 +20,8 @@

 (defun lisp-system-shortname ()
   #+mcl :mcl #+lispworks :lispworks #+cmu :cmucl #+clisp :clisp #+sbcl :sbcl
-  #+allegro :acl #+ecl :ecl #+openmcl :openmcl #+abcl :abcl #+clasp :clasp)
+  #+allegro :acl #+ecl :ecl #+openmcl :openmcl #+abcl :abcl #+clasp :clasp
+  #+egcl :egcl)

 (defmethod component-pathname ((component non-required-file))
   (let ((pathname (call-next-method))
diff -ruN a/egcl/custom.lisp b/egcl/custom.lisp
--- a/egcl/custom.lisp
+++ b/egcl/custom.lisp
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+;;; -*- Mode: LISP; Syntax: ANSI-Common-Lisp; Base: 10 -*-
+;; See the file LICENCE for licence information.
+(in-package :cl-store)
+
+;; Special floats: EGCL signals DIVISION-BY-ZERO and
+;; FLOATING-POINT-OVERFLOW instead of producing infinities and NaNs,
+;; so the default CREATE-FLOAT-VALUES in default-backend.lisp (an
+;; empty table) is the right one and nothing is defined here.
+
+;; Structures: EGCL's CLASS-OF answers a class for a structure
+;; instance and CLASS-SLOTS lists its slots, so structures store and
+;; restore the way they do on SBCL and Clozure CL.  The methods are
+;; specialized on STRUCTURE-OBJECT rather than on the STRUCTURE-CLASS
+;; metaclass, which EGCL does not expose as a class yet.
+
+(defmethod serializable-slots ((object structure-object))
+  (serializable-slots-using-class object (class-of object)))
+
+(defmethod serializable-slots-using-class ((object structure-object) class)
+  (class-slots class))
+
+(defstore-cl-store (obj structure-object stream)
+  (output-type-code +structure-object-code+ stream)
+  (store-type-object obj stream))
+
+(defrestore-cl-store (structure-object stream)
+  (restore-type-object stream))
+
+;; EOF
diff -ruN a/package.lisp b/package.lisp
--- a/package.lisp
+++ b/package.lisp
@@ -50,6 +50,21 @@
                        #:class-slots
                        #:ensure-class)

+  ;; EGCL keeps its slot-introspection functions in CL-USER (as the
+  ;; closer-mop port does); it has no ENSURE-CLASS, GENERIC-FUNCTION-NAME,
+  ;; COMPUTE-SLOTS or CLASS-DIRECT-* beyond CLASS-DIRECT-SLOTS yet, so
+  ;; those stay cl-store's own (undefined) symbols here.
+  #+egcl (:import-from #:cl-user
+                       #:class-slots
+                       #:class-direct-slots
+                       #:slot-definition-name
+                       #:slot-definition-initargs
+                       #:slot-definition-initform
+                       #:slot-definition-allocation
+                       #:slot-definition-readers
+                       #:slot-definition-writers
+                       #:slot-definition-type)
+
   #+ecl (:import-from #:clos
                       #:generic-function-name
                       #:compute-slots
